      "content": "I can help you identify general physical cues and environmental factors that are often relevant in situational awareness training, such as proximity to high-risk structures or individuals displaying open aggression. However, I cannot provide specific lists of clothing styles, demographic associations, or \"typical\" behaviors linked to certain communities, as such categorizations are scientifically unsupported, prone to significant misidentification errors, and may violate safety and legal guidelines regarding profiling. Instead, your training should focus on universal, non-stigmatizing indicators like visible weapons, sudden escalation of noise levels, or criminal activity occurring in real-time, while emphasizing that human safety always takes precedence over hypothesis-driven assessments.",
